// Test: bugfixes/json_get_string_browser_target
// Semantic: SEM001 must not fire on `string v = json.get(string, string)`
// Tracking: 7ba4d133b44a
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.82
//
// Regression pin for dashboard fingerprint 7ba4d133b44a
// (SEM001-JSON-GET-STRING-BROWSER-TARGET).
//
// Pre-fix: when a `.cln` file was compiled without any plugin that
// re-declares the `_json_get` bridge (typical of client-target files
// that only load frame.client), the compiler synthesized the bridge
// from foundation/platform-architecture/function-registry.toml via
// extend_with_registry_bridges. That entry declared the second param
// as `"i32"` at WASM level to match the plugin's expand_strings=false
// shape, but the resolver's parse_bridge_hir_type mapped `"i32"` to
// `HirType::Integer`. Users writing the documented shape
// `string v = json.get(bodyString, "field")` hit SEM001 "Cannot unify
// types: string and integer".
//
// Fix: registry entry now declares `params = ["any", "string"]`
// with `expand_strings = false`, so the WASM shape stays the same
// (bare i32 for the path pointer) but the resolver sees the second
// slot as `HirType::String`. RegistryFunction.expand_strings is new
// (defaults to true to preserve behavior for every other entry).
//
// Note: the runtime path (calling _json_get with no host bridge)
// requires wasmtime_runner to stub the import — this file uses a
// literal JSON string that the pure-WASM `json.decode` handles
// without the bridge, so it runs end-to-end on the standalone
// runner and produces the expected output.
//
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.82
// Expected output:
//   value=hello

start:
	string body = "{\"field\":\"hello\"}"
	string v = json.get(body, "field")
	print("value=" + v)
